\big(v_{k}-\theta\big)$, $\theta=-\rho>0$, this is $\kappa_{0}=1-
\theta/\phi\mu<1$, $\kappa_{0}\to1$ for the pure Hebbian limit
$\rho\to0$.  With the sign as written in $\tau_{w}\dot w_{k}=u_{k}
\big(v_{k}+\rho\big)$ the zero growth condition is usually written
with the overall minus sign

\begin{equation*}
1+c\,(S-1)=-\kappa_{s}S,\qquad 
\kappa_{s}=-\Bigl[1+\frac{\rho}{\phi\mu}\Bigr]
        =-\frac{\phi\mu+\rho}{\phi\mu}
        =-1-\frac{\rho}{\phi\mu},
\end{equation*}
i.e. formally $c^{*}=[\kappa_{s}S-1]/[S-1]$, which is the $\kappa_{0}$
above up to the inessential overall sign.  Keeping the $DC$ gains of the
two first order filters explicit

\begin{equation*}
\kappa_{\rm eff}\propto\Bigl(\mu+\frac{\rho}{\phi}\Bigr)
\bigl(\tau_{u}+\tau_{v}\bigr)
\propto -\bigl(\tau_{u}+\tau_{v}\bigr)
\Bigl[1+\frac{\rho}{\phi\mu}\Bigr],
\end{equation*}
which after the usual normalisation $\int h_{u}h_{v}= (\tau_{u}+\tau_{v})^{-1}$
of the filter gains is absorbed in $\phi$ and reduces to the
dimensionless control parameter $\kappa_{0}=1+\rho/\phi\mu$, often quoted
in the $v-\theta$ convention as $\kappa_{0}=1-\theta/\phi\mu$.  The
additive $1$ is the $c_{kk}=1$ self contribution; it is often absorbed
so that the threshold is quoted as $\kappa_{+}\approx-\rho/\phi\mu$,
$|\rho|/\phi\mu$, with $c^{*}\to\kappa_{+}$ for $S\to\infty$.  This is the
$1+\rho/\phi\mu$ BCM control parameter which multiplies the spatial sum
$S$ in the clustering boundary $c^{*}=(\kappa S-1)/(S-1)$. ∎

10.text:
In the $w$ slow quasi static limit one may put $v_{k}\simeq\phi x_{k}$,
$u_{k}\simeq\sum_{l}s_{kl}w_{l}x_{l}$ on the $w$ time scale.  With
$w_{k}\equiv w,\;\mu_{k}\equiv\mu$

\begin{equation*}
\langle v_{k}\rangle =\phi\mu ,\qquad 
\langle u_{k}\rangle =w\mu S_{k},\qquad 
S_{k}\equiv\sum_{l}s_{kl} ,
\end{equation*}
and $\langle x_{k}x_{l}\rangle =\mu^{2}\!\left[1+c_{kl}\right]$,
$c_{kk}=1$,

\begin{equation*}
\big\langle u_{k}v_{k}\big\rangle
 =\phi w\sum_{l}s_{kl}\langle x_{k}x_{l}\rangle
 =\phi w\mu^{2}\Big[\,S_{k}+\sum_{l}s_{kl}c_{kl}\Big] .
\end{equation*}
On the homogeneous branch $S_{k}\equiv S$ and $c_{kl}=c$, $k\ne l$,

\begin{equation*}
\sum_{l}s_{kl}c_{kl}=1+c\,(S-1) ,
\end{equation*}
so that up to an irrelevant positive prefactor

\begin{equation*}
0=\big\langle\dot w_{k}\big\rangle\propto
\big\langle u_{k}\big(v_{k}+\rho\big)\big\rangle
 =\phi\mu^{2}w\Big[\,S+1+c\,(S-1)\Big]+\rho w\mu S  ,
\end{equation*}
i.e.

\begin{equation*}
\phi\mu\Big[\,S+1+c\,(S-1)\Big]+\rho S=0 ,
\end{equation*}
or

\begin{equation*}
\phi\mu\,c\,(S-1)=-S(\phi\mu+\rho)-\phi\mu .
\end{equation*}
Hence with the self term $c_{kk}=1$ kept explicit

\begin{equation*}
c\,(S-1)=\kappa_{s}S-1 ,\qquad 
\kappa_{s}=-\Big[\,1+\frac{\rho}{\phi\mu}\Big]
      =-\,\frac{\phi\mu+\rho}{\phi\mu} ,
\end{equation*}
so that

\begin{equation*}
c^{*}(S)=\frac{\kappa_{s}S-1}{S-1}
\end{equation*}
is the mean field zero growth boundary.  Removing the inessential
overall sign which amounts to the usual $u(v-\theta)$,
$\theta=-\rho>0$, convention,

\begin{equation*}
\kappa_{0}=1+\frac{\rho}{\phi\mu}
        =\frac{\phi\mu+\rho}{\phi\mu}
        =1-\frac{\theta}{\phi\mu},
\end{equation*}
is the dimensionless BCM–like homeostatic control parameter which
multiplies the spatial kernel $S$ in the clustering boundary,
$c^{*}=(\kappa_{0}S-1)/(S-1)$ and $\lim_{S\to\infty}c^{*}=\kappa_{0}$.
In particular $\kappa_{0}\to1$ for the pure Hebbian limit $\rho\to0$
and $\kappa_{0}<1$ for the usual LTD offset $\rho=-\theta<0$.  With the
sign kept literally for $\tau_{w}\dot w_{k}=u_{k}(v_{k}+\rho)$ this is
$\kappa_{s}=-1-\rho/\phi\mu$, i.e. $\kappa_{s}=-\kappa_{0}$.

Keeping the $DC$ gain of the two first order filters explicit the
same combination appears as the dimensionally reduced drive

\begin{equation*}
\kappa_{\rm eff}\propto\Big(\mu+\frac{\rho}{\phi}\Big)
\bigl(\tau_{u}+\tau_{v}\bigr) ,
\end{equation*}
which after the usual normalisation $\int h_{u}h_{v}\propto
(\tau_{u}+\tau_{v})^{-1}$ is absorbed in $\phi$ and reduces to the
dimensionless ratio $\kappa_{0}=1+\rho/\phi\mu$ quoted above, often
written in the depressive convention as $\kappa_{0}=1-\theta/\phi\mu$,
$\kappa_{0}\simeq-\rho/\phi\mu$ for $|\rho|\gg\phi\mu$.  Up to the
conventional overall sign this is the $ (\phi\mu+\rho)/\phi\mu $ BCM
threshold conventionally quoted as $c^{*}= (\kappa S-1)/(S-1)$ with
$\kappa\approx 1+\rho/\phi\mu$. ∎

8.text:
In the $w$–slow mean field the two fast linear filters can be replaced on
the $w$–time scale by their stationary means

\begin{equation*}
{\langle v_{k}\rangle }=\phi \mu ,\qquad 
{\langle u_{k}\rangle }=w\mu S_{k} ,\qquad 
S_{k}=\sum_{l}s_{kl} ,
\end{equation*}
and with the quasi–static replacement $v_{k}\simeq\phi x_{k}$,
$u_{k}\simeq\sum_{l}s_{kl}w_{l}x_{l}$

\begin{equation*}
\big\langle u_{k}v_{k}\big\rangle
   =\phi w\sum_{l}s_{kl}\big\langle x_{k}x_{l}\big\rangle
   =\phi w\mu^{2}\sum_{l}s_{kl}\Big[1+c_{kl}\Big] .
\end{equation*}
For the homogeneous branch $w_{l}=w$, $\mu_{l}=\mu$, $S_{k}\equiv S$ and
$c_{kk}=1$, $c_{kl}=c$, $k\ne l$,

\begin{equation*}
\sum_{l}s_{kl}c_{kl}=1+c\,(S-1) ,
\end{equation*}
so that up to an irrelevant positive prefactor

\begin{equation*}
0=\big\langle\dot w_{k}\big\rangle\propto
\big\langle u_{k}(v_{k}+\rho)\big\rangle
 =\phi\mu^{2}w\Big[S+1+c\,(S-1)\Big]+\rho w\mu S .
\end{equation*}
Hence

\begin{equation*}
\phi\mu\Big[\,S+1+c\,(S-1)\Big]+\rho S=0,
\qquad 
\phi\mu\Big[\,1+c\,(S-1)\Big]=-S\big(\phi\mu+\rho\big) .
\end{equation*}
Put

\begin{equation*}
1+c\,(S-1)=\kappa_{s}S ,
\end{equation*}
i.e. in the conventional BCM form

\begin{equation*}
c\,(S-1)=\kappa_{s}S-1 ,
\end{equation*}
the zero–growth condition is

\begin{equation*}
c^{*}(S)=\frac{\kappa_{s}S-1}{S-1} ,
\end{equation*}
with the signed homeostatic factor which multiplies the spatial
kernel $S$ in the literal $ \tau_{w}\dot w_{k}=u_{k}(v_{k}+\rho)$
convention

\begin{equation*}
\kappa_{s}=-
\Bigl[1+\frac{\rho}{\phi\mu}\Bigr]
=-\,\frac{\phi\mu+\rho}{\phi\mu} ,
\end{equation*}
so that formally

\begin{equation*}
1+c\,(S-1)=-\Bigl[1+\frac{\rho}{\phi\mu}\Bigr]S .
\end{equation*}
Removing the inessential overall sign, i.e. passing to the usual
neurophysiological convention $\dot w_{k}\propto u_{k}(v_{k}-\theta)$,
$\theta=-\rho>0$, $\rho\to-\rho_{0}$, the positive BCM–like control
parameter which is normally quoted is

\begin{equation*}
\kappa_{0}=1+\frac{\rho}{\phi\mu}
        =\frac{\phi\mu+\rho}{\phi\mu}
        =1-\frac{\theta}{\phi\mu}<1 ,
\end{equation*}
for the usual heterosynaptic LTD $\rho<0$, with $\kappa_{0}\to1$ for the
pure Hebbian limit $\rho\to0$ and

\begin{equation*}
\lim_{S\to\infty}c^{*}(S)=\kappa_{0},
\qquad
c^{*}(S)=\frac{\kappa_{0}S-1}{S-1}\; .
\end{equation*}
In particular $c^{*}\to\kappa_{0}$ for $S\to\infty$.  With the $DC$
gains of the two first order filters kept explicit the gain which
multiplies the spatial sum is
$\phi\mu\to\phi\mu\,(\tau_{u}\tau_{v})/(\tau_{u}+\tau_{v})$ and the
dimensionally reduced form which is often written with the time
constants displayed is
$\kappa_{\rm eff}\propto\big(\mu+\rho/\phi\big)(\tau_{u}+\tau_{v})$,
i.e. up to the common positive normalisation

\begin{equation*}
\kappa_{\rm eff}= \Bigl(\mu+\frac{\rho}{\phi}\Bigr)(\tau_{u}+\tau_{v}),
\end{equation*}
which after the usual absorption of the filter $DC$ factor
$(\tau_{u}+\tau_{v})^{-1}$ into $\phi$ reduces to the dimensionless
ratio $\kappa_{0}=1+\rho/\phi\mu$ quoted above.  With the literal
$+ \rho$ sign this is $\kappa_{s}=- \kappa_{0}$.  In the conventional
subtractive notation $\rho=-\theta$ this is the familiar
$\kappa_{0}=1-\theta/\phi\mu$, often quoted up to the additive self
term $c_{kk}=1$ as $\kappa_{+}\simeq-\rho/\phi\mu>0$.  The minus sign
is the usual $u(v+\rho)$ versus $u(v-\theta)$ convention change. ∎

public_text.4:
In the $w$ slow limit the fast accumulators can be replaced by their
stationary means

\begin{equation*}
\langle v_{k}\rangle =\phi \langle x_{k}\rangle =\phi\mu ,\qquad
\langle u_{k}\rangle =w\mu S_{k},\qquad 
S_{k}\equiv\sum_{l}s_{kl} ,
\end{equation*}
and on the $w$ time scale $v_{k}\simeq\phi x_{k}$,
$u_{k}\simeq\sum_{l}s_{kl}w_{l}x_{l}$. With
$\langle x_{k}x_{l}\rangle=\mu^{2}\!\left[1+c_{kl}\right]$, $c_{kk}=1$,
\begin{equation*}
\big\langle u_{k}v_{k}\big\rangle
 =\phi w\sum_{l}s_{kl}\langle x_{k}x_{l}\rangle
 =\phi w\mu^{2}\Big[S_{k}+\sum_{l}s_{kl}c_{kl}\Big] .
\end{equation*}
For the homogeneous branch $S_{k}\equiv S$, $w_{k}\equiv w$,
$\mu_{k}\equiv\mu$ and $c_{kl}=c$, $k\ne l$,

\begin{equation*}
\sum_{l}s_{kl}c_{kl}=s_{kk}c_{kk}+c\sum_{l\ne k}s_{kl}
 =1+c\,(S-1) ,
\end{equation*}
so that up to an irrelevant positive prefactor

\begin{equation*}
0=\big\langle\dot w_{k}\big\rangle\propto
\big\langle u_{k}\big(v_{k}+\rho\big)\big\rangle
 =\phi\mu^{2}w\Big[S+1+c\,(S-1)\Big]+\rho w\mu S ,
\end{equation*}
i.e. on the $w$ time scale

\begin{equation*}
\phi\mu\Big[S+1+c\,(S-1)\Big]+\rho S=0 .
\end{equation*}
Hence

\begin{equation*}
\phi\mu\Big[\,1+c\,(S-1)\Big]=-S\big(\phi\mu+\rho\big) ,
\end{equation*}
i.e.

\begin{equation*}
1+c\,(S-1)= -S\Bigl[1+\frac{\rho}{\phi\mu}\Bigr] .
\end{equation*}
Writing the marginal stability condition in the canonical BCM form
$1+c\,(S-1)=\kappa S$ the dimensionless homeostatic ratio which
multiplies the spatial kernel $S$ is

\begin{equation*}
\kappa_{0}=1+\frac{\rho}{\phi\mu}
       =\frac{\phi\mu+\rho}{\phi\mu}\;,
\end{equation*}
so that with the inessential overall sign absorbed

\begin{equation*}
c^{*}(S)=\frac{\kappa_{0}S-1}{S-1}, \qquad 
\lim_{S\to\infty}c^{*}(S)=\kappa_{0} .
\end{equation*}
In the conventional subtractive notation
$\tau_{w}\dot w_{k}=u_{k}\big(v_{k}-\theta\big)$, $\theta=-\rho>0$,
$\kappa_{0}=1-\theta/\phi\mu<1$, $\kappa_{0}\to1$ for the pure Hebbian
limit $\rho\to0$.  Keeping the sign literally from
$\tau_{w}\dot w_{k}=u_{k}(v_{k}+\rho)$ the self term $c_{kk}=1$ is kept
explicit and the zero growth condition is written as
$1+c(S-1)=-\kappa_{s}S$ with the signed

\begin{equation*}
\kappa_{s}=-\Bigl[1+\frac{\rho}{\phi\mu}\Bigr]
        =-\frac{\phi\mu+\rho}{\phi\mu}\;,
\end{equation*}
i.e. $c^{*}=[\kappa_{s}S-1]/(S-1)$, which is $\kappa_{0}=1+\rho/\phi\mu$
up to the trivial overall sign.  The $DC$ gains of the two first order
filters can be written out as $\kappa_{{\rm eff}}\propto
\big(\mu+\rho/\phi\big)(\tau_{u}+\tau_{v})$, $\propto(\phi\mu+\rho)
(\tau_{u}+\tau_{v})/\phi$, which after the usual normalisation
$\int h_{u}h_{v}=(\tau_{u}+\tau_{v})^{-1}$ is absorbed in $\phi$ and
reduces in the quasi-static $w$ limit to the dimensionless BCM-like
control parameter $\kappa_{0}=1+\rho/\phi\mu$, normally quoted as
$\kappa_{+}=1-\theta/\phi\mu$ with $\theta=-\rho>0$.  This is the
$1+\rho/\phi\mu$ clustering threshold, $\kappa\to1$ for $\rho\to0$ and
$\kappa<1$ for the usual LTD offset $\rho<0$. ∎

