8.text:
In the slow $w$ limit the fast accumulators can be closed quasi–statically
on the $w$ time scale

\begin{equation*}
v_{k}\simeq\phi x_{k},\qquad 
u_{k}\simeq\sum_{l}s_{kl}w_{l}x_{l},\qquad 
\langle x_{k}\rangle =\mu ,
\end{equation*}
so that on a homogeneous branch $w_{l}\equiv w$, $\mu_{l}\equiv\mu$,

\begin{equation*}
\langle v_{k}\rangle =\phi\mu ,\qquad 
\langle u_{k}\rangle =w\mu S,\qquad 
S\equiv S_{k}=\sum_{l}s_{kl},
\end{equation*}
and with $\langle x_{k}x_{l}\rangle =\mu^{2}\!\left[1+c_{kl}\right]$,
$c_{kk}=1$,

\begin{equation*}
\big\langle u_{k}v_{k}\big\rangle
 =\phi w\sum_{l}s_{kl}\langle x_{k}x_{l}\rangle
 =\phi w\mu^{2}\Big[S+\sum_{l}s_{kl}c_{kl}\Big] .
\end{equation*}
On the homogeneous branch $c_{kl}=c$, $k\ne l$,

\begin{equation*}
\sum_{l}s_{kl}c_{kl}=1+c\,(S-1) ,
\end{equation*}
so that up to an irrelevant positive prefactor

\begin{equation*}
0=\big\langle\dot w_{k}\big\rangle\propto
\big\langle u_{k}\big(v_{k}+\rho\big)\big\rangle
 =\phi\mu^{2}w\Big[\,S+1+c\,(S-1)\Big]+\rho w\mu S .
\end{equation*}
Hence on the $w$ time scale

\begin{equation*}
\phi\mu\Big[\,S+1+c\,(S-1)\Big]+\rho S=0,
\qquad
\phi\mu\Big[\,1+c\,(S-1)\Big]=-S\big(\phi\mu+\rho\big),
\end{equation*}
i.e.

\begin{equation*}
1+c\,(S-1)=-\,S\Bigl[1+\frac{\rho}{\phi\mu}\Bigr] .
\end{equation*}
Writing the marginal condition in the canonical BCM form
$1+c\,(S-1)=\kappa_{s}S$ the signed factor which multiplies the spatial
kernel $S$ in the literal $\tau_{w}\dot w_{k}=u_{k}(v_{k}+\rho)$ convention
is therefore

\begin{equation*}
\kappa_{s}S=1+c\,(S-1),\qquad
\kappa_{s}= -\Bigl[\,1+\frac{\rho}{\phi\mu}\Bigr]
        =-\,\frac{\phi\mu+\rho}{\phi\mu}
        =-1-\frac{\rho}{\phi\mu},
\end{equation*}
so that with the self term $c_{kk}=1$ kept explicit

\begin{equation*}
c\,(S-1)=\kappa_{s}S-1,\qquad
c^{*}(S)=\frac{\kappa_{s}S-1}{S-1},
\end{equation*}
i.e. $c^{*}=[-(1+\rho/\phi\mu)S-1]/(S-1)$.

Removing the inessential overall sign $u(v+\rho)\leftrightarrow
u(v-\theta)$, $\theta=-\rho>0$, the positive BCM–like homeostatic
control parameter which is normally quoted is

\begin{equation*}
\kappa_{0}=1+\frac{\rho}{\phi\mu}
        =\frac{\phi\mu+\rho}{\phi\mu}
        =1-\frac{\theta}{\phi\mu},
\end{equation*}
so that with the usual depressive sign $\rho=-\theta<0$

\begin{equation*}
c^{*}(S)=\frac{\kappa_{0}S-1}{S-1},\qquad 
\lim_{S\to\infty}c^{*}(S)=\kappa_{0},\qquad 
\kappa_{0}\to1\;\;{\rm for}\;\;\rho\to0,
\end{equation*}
