public_text.12:
In the $w$--slow mean field the two first order filters can be eliminated
on the $w$ time scale

\begin{equation*}
v_{k}\simeq\phi x_{k}\qquad 
u_{k}\simeq\sum_{l}s_{kl}w_{l}x_{l},
\end{equation*}
so that on the homogeneous branch $w_{l}\equiv w$, $\mu_{l}\equiv\mu$,
$S_{k}\equiv\sum_{l}s_{kl}\equiv S$

\begin{equation*}
\langle v_{k}\rangle =\phi\mu ,\qquad 
\langle u_{k}\rangle =w\mu S ,\qquad
\langle u_{k}v_{k}\rangle
 =\phi w\sum_{l}s_{kl}\langle x_{k}x_{l}\rangle .
\end{equation*}
With $\langle x_{k}x_{l}\rangle =\mu^{2}\!\left[1+c_{kl}\right]$,
$c_{kk}=1$, $c_{kl}=c$, $k\ne l$,

\begin{equation*}
\sum_{l}s_{kl}c_{kl}=1+c\,(S-1) ,
\end{equation*}
and up to an irrelevant positive prefactor

\begin{equation*}
0=\big\langle\dot w_{k}\big\rangle\propto
\big\langle u_{k}\big(v_{k}+\rho\big)\big\rangle
 =\phi\mu^{2}w\Big[S+1+c\,(S-1)\Big]+\rho w\mu S .
\end{equation*}
Hence on the slow $w$ scale

\begin{equation*}
\phi\mu\Big[S+1+c\,(S-1)\Big]+\rho S=0,
\qquad 
\phi\mu\Big[1+c\,(S-1)\Big]=-S\big(\phi\mu+\rho\big) .
\end{equation*}
Writing the marginal condition in the BCM form

\begin{equation*}
1+c\,(S-1)=\kappa_{s}S ,
\end{equation*}
the signed zero growth factor which multiplies the spatial kernel $S$
in the literal $\tau_{w}\dot w_{k}=u_{k}(v_{k}+\rho)$ convention is

\begin{equation*}
\kappa_{s}S=1+c\,(S-1),\qquad 
\kappa_{s}= -\Bigl[\,1+\frac{\rho}{\phi\mu}\Bigr]
       =-\,\frac{\phi\mu+\rho}{\phi\mu}
       =-1-\frac{\rho}{\phi\mu},
\end{equation*}
so that with the self term $c_{kk}=1$ kept explicit

\begin{equation*}
c^{*}(S)=\frac{\kappa_{s}S-1}{S-1},\qquad
c^{*}(S)=\frac{-\bigl[1+\rho/\phi\mu\bigr]S-1}{S-1},
\end{equation*}
i.e. $1+c\,(S-1)=-\,[1+\rho/\phi\mu]\,S$.
Removing the inessential overall sign, $\dot w_{k}\propto u_{k}(v_{k}-\theta)$,
$\theta=-\rho>0$, the positive BCM–like control parameter normally
quoted is

\begin{equation*}
\kappa_{0}=1+\frac{\rho}{\phi\mu}
       =\frac{\phi\mu+\rho}{\phi\mu}
       =1-\frac{\theta}{\phi\mu},
\end{equation*}
so that with the conventional subtractive sign

\begin{equation*}
c^{*}(S)=\frac{\kappa_{0}S-1}{S-1},\qquad
\lim_{S\to\infty}c^{*}(S)=\kappa_{0},
\end{equation*}
$\kappa_{0}\to1$ for the pure Hebbian limit $\rho\to0$ and
$\kappa_{0}<1$ for the usual LTD offset $\rho=-\theta<0$.  In the LTD
convention this is the familiar $\kappa_{0}=1-\theta/\phi\mu$, often
written up to the additive self term as $\kappa_{+}\simeq-\rho/\phi\mu$.

