sign, $u(v+\rho)\leftrightarrow u(v-\theta)$, $\theta=-\rho>0$, the
positive BCM–like control parameter which multiplies the spatial kernel
$S$ is

\begin{equation*}
\kappa_{0}=1+\frac{\rho}{\phi\mu}
       =\frac{\phi\mu+\rho}{\phi\mu}
       =1-\frac{\theta}{\phi\mu}>0,
\end{equation*}
so that with the usual subtractive convention

\begin{equation*}
c^{*}(S)=\frac{\kappa_{0}S-1}{S-1},\qquad 
\lim_{S\to\infty}c^{*}(S)=\kappa_{0},
\end{equation*}
$\kappa_{0}\to1$ for the pure Hebbian limit $\rho\to0$ and
$\kappa_{0}<1$ for the usual LTD offset $\rho=-\theta<0$.  In particular
$v_{k}+\rho\to\phi\mu+\rho=\phi\big(\mu+\rho/\phi\big)$ is the
homogeneous drive which multiplies the spatial sum $S$.

Keeping the DC gains of the two first order filters explicit the drive
which multiplies $S$ is written in dimensional form as

\begin{equation*}
\kappa_{\rm eff}\propto\Bigl(\mu+\frac{\rho}{\phi}\Bigr)
\bigl(\tau_{u}+\tau_{v}\bigr)
\propto\frac{\phi\mu+\rho}{\phi}\bigl(\tau_{u}+\tau_{v}\bigr),
\end{equation*}
i.e. up to the common positive normalisation
$\int h_{u}h_{v}\propto(\tau_{u}+\tau_{v})^{-1}$ absorbed in the definition
of $\phi$

\begin{equation*}
\kappa=\Bigl(\mu+\frac{\rho}{\phi}\Bigr)\bigl(\tau_{u}+\tau_{v}\bigr)
\;\propto\;\phi\mu+\rho ,
\end{equation*}
which after the usual absorption of the filter overlap reduces to the
dimensionless BCM ratio $\kappa_{0}=(\phi\mu+\rho)/\phi\mu=
1+\rho/\phi\mu$.  With the sign kept literally for $\tau_{w}\dot w_{k}=
u_{k}(v_{k}+\rho)$ this is $\kappa_{s}=-\kappa_{0}=-1-\rho/\phi\mu$,
$c^{*}=(\kappa_{s}S-1)/(S-1)$, the conventionally quoted positive form
being $\kappa_{0}=1+\rho/\phi\mu$, often written in the $v-\theta$
convention as $\kappa_{0}=1-\theta/\phi\mu\simeq-\rho/\phi\mu$ for
$|\rho|\gg\phi\mu$.  This is the homeostatic parameter which controls
the clustering boundary $c^{*}=(\kappa S-1)/(S-1)$. ∎
